---
import ResidenceLayout from "../../../layouts/ResidenceLayout.astro";
import { frederick, frederickPhotos } from "../../../data/residences/frederick";
---

<ResidenceLayout
  residence={frederick}
  title="Resident handbook · Frederick Cottage | Mt Cottages"
  description="Frederick Cottage resident handbook: expectations, policies, payments, maintenance, and emergency guidance."
  eyebrow="Frederick Cottage · Handbook"
  heading="The handbook for living here."
  lede="Expectations, policies, and support paths — written for the resident, kept general where arrangements vary."
  hero={frederickPhotos.living}
>
  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="site-width prose">
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Living here well</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Frederick Cottage hosts furnished stays with a 30-day minimum stay. Treat it as a home on a residential street: tidy entry and lawn rhythm, considerate noise, and care for furnishings, kitchen, and laundry.</p>
          <ul><li>Kitchen: clean as you go; confirm consumables, dishwasher, and trash placement.</li><li>Laundry: confirm machine use, supplies, and lint/dryer care on arrival.</li><li>Outdoors: keep entry clear; confirm grill, furniture, and yard expectations.</li><li>Smoking, guests, and pets follow the written arrangement — ask before assuming.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Policies</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>An inquiry is a conversation, not a lease or approval. Any later screening, agreement, payment schedule, or approval is a separate step with its own documents.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Stay length: 30-day minimum stay as the baseline; short-term pricing by inquiry.</li>
            <li>Payments: use the instructions tied to the agreement; never email card or bank details.</li>
            <li>Privacy: do not submit Social Security numbers or sensitive documents via the public form. A stay inquiry may include contact details, timing, household size, preferred community, budget, pets, accessibility needs, and reason for the stay. Mt Cottages uses those details to respond, compare options, and coordinate next steps. Inquiry information is retained only as long as reasonably necessary. To ask about access, correction, or deletion, email stay@mtcottages.com.</li>
            <li>Common questions: an inquiry is the right place to ask about availability, pricing, pets, accessibility, and arrangement specifics.</li>
            <li>Household: occupants, pets, and accessibility needs agreed in advance.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Maintenance & emergencies</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>For non-emergency issues: submit a clear request with the home, location, problem, timing, and photos only when they help explain the issue without exposing private information. Describe what happened, where it is, when it started, and whether it affects safety or ordinary use. Email <a class="text-link" href="mailto:stay@mtcottages.com?subject=Maintenance%20request">stay@mtcottages.com</a> with subject "Maintenance request".</p>
          <p>For immediate danger — fire, active gas smell, flooding that will cause immediate damage, or any other immediate danger — call 911 or the appropriate emergency service first. After immediate safety is handled, contact the resident support channel provided for your home and explain what happened. Do not send payment-card numbers, bank credentials, Social Security numbers, or other sensitive information by ordinary email.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Payments & portal</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Current residents use the portal, rent, and support paths tied to their agreement. Links stay general here because methods vary by arrangement.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Resident portal: portal access is provided directly to current residents. If you need the correct link, contact stay@mtcottages.com from the email associated with your stay.</li>
            <li>Payments: use the secure payment instructions provided for your agreement. Payment methods can vary by home and arrangement — contact Mt Cottages if you need the correct link or instructions.</li>
            <li>Never send card numbers, bank credentials, or sensitive identity information through ordinary email.</li>
            <li>Home support: use the maintenance path above for non-emergency issues and the emergency guidance for immediate danger.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</ResidenceLayout>
